  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1223 PM MDT Tue Aug 18 2026\n\nAn elongated high pressure system persists to our south today, \nplacing a stream of mild moisture across the northern portions \nof our CWA. Here, some showers have already developed with some \nisolated thunderstorms expected to form this afternoon over the \neastern Uintas and possibly into the Yampa River Basin. Impacts \nshould be minimal with these storms aside from a few gusty \noutflow winds given the relatively dry near-surface layer. Even\nas the ridge builds tomorrow and into Thursday, moisture \nremains trapped west of the Rockies, maintaining daily chances \nof showers and thunderstorms focused over the high terrain. \nThere's no indication that the low-level atmosphere will come \nclose to saturating through the work week, so heavy rainfall \npotential is fairly low. However, given the weakening flow \naloft, storm motion could come to a screeching halt by Thursday,\nwhich means the potential for a localized flash flood concern \nover vulnerable areas is non-negligible. Still, this is an \nunlikely scenario. What is likely with this building ridge is \nthe return of high temperatures ~10 degrees above normal, \nleaving some low-lying areas to hit triple digit highs once \nagain.\n\nInto the weekend, deterministic models are suggesting an omega \nblock forms across the country, leaving us firmly underneath \nsouthwesterly flow. Under this, there is an emerging signal of \nanother round of monsoonal moisture working its way into the \nGreat Basin. At this time, indications are that the plume is not\noverly strong nor wide in areal extent, and so it's iffy on how\nconcerning heavy rain impacts could be. However, even if the \ncenter of the moisture plume skirts around us, we are expecting \nsome amount of an uptick in storm coverage. Further speculation \non impacts will depend on storm motion, the potential for \ntraining storms, and instability resulting from cloud cover (or \nthe lack thereof), all of which are too early to speak on with \nconfidence at this time. Once hi-res model guidance becomes \navailable in a couple days, these details will become clearer. \nUntil then, keep this weekend in the back of your mind as the \nnext potentially potent weather day.",
